  "derivation": "Expected runtimes were obtained by deploying the site's embedded creation bytecode + router arg on a local paris EVM (ganache, hardfork 'merge') and reading eth_getCode; router() on the local deployments returned the correct router for both chains; deploy gas used was 1,210,012 for each.",
  "knownDiscrepancy_metadataHashOnly": "A fresh solc 0.8.26 build (optimizer 200, paris) of the current repo source reproduces the embedded creation bytecode byte-for-byte EXCEPT the 32-byte CBOR metadata (IPFS) hash at the very end (58 of its 64 hex chars differ; everything else, including the 'solc 0.8.26' version tail, is identical). Same for the runtime: a fresh build patched at the immutable slots matches the embedded-bytecode runtime except the runtime's copy of that hash. The .sol file is byte-identical to the version committed with the bytecode (git: unchanged since 93800f0, the v7 commit), so the difference lies in the original build frontend's metadata inputs (source-unit naming / settings serialisation), which could not be reproduced with solc-js standard JSON across the variants tried (bare name, contracts/ path, ./-prefixed, absolute path, literal-content, explicit optimizer details, CRLF/newline variants). Executable code is provably identical; the metadata hash is never executed. The baseline above is anchored to the site's embedded bytecode (what users actually deploy), so post-deploy verification is unaffected. Flagged for a decision: leave as-is, or regenerate SplitSwap.json + SPLIT_BYTECODE from the current source (would change only the metadata hash) to make the repo self-reproducing.",
